From: a50-halium <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] build.sh: make the ramdisk cpio deterministic

The ramdisk is an uncompressed newc cpio built straight from a directory in
the source tree. Two things in that pipeline vary between machines and make
two builds of the same source produce different boot images:

  * `find .` walks in filesystem order, so archive entry order depends on how
    the checkout happened to land on disk.
  * GNU cpio writes each file's real inode number into the newc header.

Sorting the file list fixes the ordering, and --renumber-inodes replaces the
inode numbers with a sequence starting from a fixed value. File mtimes are the
third source and are normalised by build/build-kernel.sh before this runs,
since those come from the filesystem rather than from this command.

With all three closed, the boot image hashes identically across machines.

--- a/build.sh
+++ b/build.sh
@@ -221,7 +221,7 @@ BUILD_RAMDISK() {
     script_echo "Compression type: $comptype"
 
     cd "$TOP/tools/make/ramdisk" || exit
-    find . | cpio -R 0:0 -H newc --quiet -o | $compcmd > "$TOP/tools/make/$RAMDISK"
+    find . | LC_ALL=C sort | cpio -R 0:0 -H newc --renumber-inodes --quiet -o | $compcmd > "$TOP/tools/make/$RAMDISK"
     cd "$TOP" || exit
 
     if [ ! -f "$TOP/tools/make/$RAMDISK" ]; then
